Memory Map
The CPU accesses memory and peripheral registers using addresses.

Address region 		Purpose
0x08000000			Internal Flash- program storage
0x20000000			SRAM- runtime variables, stack, heap
0x40000000			Peripheral register address region
0xE0000000 			Cortex-M system control and debug region

What happens when you access an address?
</> Flash - 0x080000000
Your firmware instructions are stored here and normally execute from Flash. 
Flash is non-volatile and read-only at runtime.

</> SRAM - 0x20000000
Runtime data such as variables, buffers, stacks, resides here.
SRAM is fast, writable, and erased on every reset.

</> Peripherals - 0x40000000
Reading or writing the appropriate address lets firmware interact with hardware registers.

volatile: "re-read from memory every time, never optimize away." Every peripheral register and 
every ISR-shared variable must be volatile. 

